## Why
The step definition `^the service (?:answers|replies) "([^"]+)"$` (`tests/mcp/steps/mcp_steps.go:24`) is reached by two catalogue templates:

- `the service answers "{reply}"` (matched by E2E-001's step `the service answers "pong"`)
- `the service replies "{reply}"` (matched by E2E-002's step `the service replies "hello"`)

Both entries already carry the identical meaning — *The MCP service's reply to the message is exactly the quoted text.* — and one definition binds both phrasings, so "answers" and "replies" are two words for the same step, not two different steps. The catalogue must say that once: merge the two entries into a single entry whose template offers both literal words as alternatives (`[answers|replies]`), so the one definition is reached by exactly one template.

